      "title": "Stuck Sync-Lock Debugging",
      "lang": "Go",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "goal": "Debug a coupon syncer where one API failure permanently wedges the in-flight lock and aborts the whole batch. Fix sync.go only; tests are read-only.",
      "signal": "Root-cause debugging, not feature writing: two interacting bugs (early return skips lock release, one bad coupon halts the batch) mirror a real cart gift-sync incident. Hidden concurrency tests catch superficial fixes."
    },
    {
      "name": "go-currency-market",
      "title": "Currency \u0026 Market Mapping",
      "lang": "Go",
      "difficulty": "Medium",
      "goal": "Implement ISO 4217 minor-unit money formatting (0/2/3 decimal currencies, negatives) and currency-to-country market mapping from a written spec.",
      "signal": "Pure spec-to-code fidelity under fintech edge cases: JPY has no decimals, KWD has three, -70 cents must render -0.70. Models that skim the spec fail on exponent edge cases."
    },
    {
      "name": "go-graphql-optional-field",
      "title": "Optional GraphQL Field Fallback",
      "lang": "Go",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "goal": "Query an optional GraphQL field for market support, but degrade gracefully when the API version rejects it: retry once without the field, propagate every other error.",
      "signal": "Recreates a real 3-day production outage: an agent added presentmentCurrencies to a discount query, older API versions rejected the whole query, and the handler swallowed the failure. Tests schema-evolution defensiveness — distinguishing 'field not supported' from real errors and never silently succeeding."
    },
    {
      "name": "go-portlist",
      "title": "lsof Output Parser",
      "lang": "Go",
      "difficulty": "Medium",
      "goal": "Parse raw `lsof -F pcn` field output into structured listeners: pid/command blocks with multiple addresses, IPv6 brackets, malformed lines, and exact-duplicate dedupe.",
      "signal": "Real-world messy-text parsing from a dev-tools CLI. Punishes models that pattern-match a happy path instead of reading the field format: stateful blocks, skip rules, and order preservation trip up weaker models."
    },
    {
      "name": "go-webhook-retry",
      "title": "Webhook Retry Semantics",
      "lang": "Go",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "goal": "Fix a Shopify-style webhook handler that returns HTTP 200 even when processing fails, and rejects nothing on HMAC mismatch.",
      "signal": "Distilled from a real production incident where broken discount syncs went silent for 3 days. Tests whether a model understands delivery/retry contracts and auth-before-processing — not just making code compile. The most discriminating task in the suite."
    },
